<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mahayana Buddhism</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mahayana</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mahayana <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a> is a major branch of Buddhism emphasising the bodhisattva ideal and a broad body of scriptures. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya</a> was an important centre of Mahayana learning, attracting pilgrims and scholars. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer Empire</a>, Mahayana Buddhism was promoted notably by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jayavarman-vii">Jayavarman VII</a> alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> traditions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mahayana-buddhism.jpg" alt="Mahayana Buddhism" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: World Imaging · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BuddhistTriad.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
